WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:04.849
- Space is an incredibly dangerous place.

00:00:04.849 --> 00:00:07.146
If you do something wrong, it's game over,

00:00:07.146 --> 00:00:09.479
so the stakes are very high.

00:00:11.747 --> 00:00:15.587
To keep everyone safe,
we practice routinely

00:00:15.587 --> 00:00:17.780
emergency procedures.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.686
I think the biggest emergency is

00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:23.876
is loss of depress, or depressurization.

00:00:23.876 --> 00:00:27.310
If something's coming at you
and hits the Space Station

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:28.784
then that's gonna cause a breach.

00:00:28.784 --> 00:00:31.089
And it can be something as
small as two centimeters

00:00:31.089 --> 00:00:34.502
in diameter that could do a lot of damage.

00:00:34.502 --> 00:00:37.581
Everyone would go to
their respective vehicle

00:00:37.581 --> 00:00:39.784
and close the hatches
because initially, if it's

00:00:39.784 --> 00:00:42.456
very fast, you only have so much time

00:00:42.456 --> 00:00:44.273
to get in that vehicle safely

00:00:44.273 --> 00:00:46.273
and be ready to go home.

00:00:47.363 --> 00:00:50.461
Another situation we train for is

00:00:50.461 --> 00:00:51.670
fire.

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:53.470
If a fire alarm goes off

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:56.210
on our computer screen you would see

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:59.118
the actual module where
the smoke detectors

00:00:59.118 --> 00:01:00.886
think you're seeing a fire.

00:01:00.886 --> 00:01:02.375
And then you would actually
physically go there

00:01:02.375 --> 00:01:04.735
to see if you actually
have identified smoke,

00:01:04.735 --> 00:01:08.189
or flames, or anything coming out.

00:01:08.189 --> 00:01:11.590
And the solar flare, the sun kind of burps

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:14.539
every so often, and sends
out high energy particles

00:01:14.539 --> 00:01:15.422
from the sun.

00:01:15.422 --> 00:01:18.774
The dangers around solar
flares are that you can

00:01:18.774 --> 00:01:21.476
accumulate too much
radiation in your body.

00:01:21.476 --> 00:01:24.178
If there's a solar flare,
all of the astronauts float

00:01:24.178 --> 00:01:25.987
up into the doghouse, we call it

00:01:25.987 --> 00:01:28.497
that has a ton of water bags

00:01:28.497 --> 00:01:29.623
surrounding it.

00:01:29.623 --> 00:01:32.215
And the water will absorb
and keep the radiation

00:01:32.215 --> 00:01:33.597
from coming into our bodies.

00:01:33.597 --> 00:01:35.292
And we can just wait until

00:01:35.292 --> 00:01:38.746
Houston gives us the call
to say everything's clear.

00:01:38.746 --> 00:01:42.008
As astronauts, you're
trained to not be alarmed

00:01:42.008 --> 00:01:42.841
by things.

00:01:42.841 --> 00:01:45.300
You're trained to go into a mode of

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.579
how will I save the day,

00:01:46.579 --> 00:01:47.514
how will I fix this,

00:01:47.514 --> 00:01:49.575
how will I do all the steps required

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:52.795
to make sure that, you know, we come home safely?

00:01:52.795 --> 00:01:55.378
(gentle music)

